{"framework":"vue","displayName":"Accessories And Menus ▸ Import from Excel · Standard example · Vue 3","tier":2,"engine":"container","sandpackTemplate":null,"sandpackEnvironment":null,"container":"vue","htWrappers":["@handsontable/vue3"],"entry":"/src/main.ts","htmlEntry":"/index.html","devCommand":"pnpm exec vite --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173","buildCommand":"vite build","outputDir":"dist","outputGlob":null,"staticExport":false,"spaMode":false,"port":5173,"installCommand":"pnpm install","htCoreRange":"0.0.0-next-36242d6-20261027","fileCount":5,"assets":[],"skipped":[],"files":{"/package.json":"{\n  \"name\": \"handsontable-vue-example\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"packageManager\": \"pnpm@10.34.5\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"handsontable\": \"0.0.0-next-36242d6-20261027\",\n    \"@handsontable/vue3\": \"0.0.0-next-36242d6-20261027\",\n    \"vue\": \"3.x\",\n    \"vite\": \"^5.4.0\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-vue\": \"^5.0.0\",\n    \"hyperformula\": \"3.5.0\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\"\n  }\n}","/vite.config.js":"import { defineConfig } from \"vite\";\nimport vue from \"@vitejs/plugin-vue\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({ plugins: [vue()], server: { allowedHosts: true } });","/index.html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Handsontable Vue Example</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"example1\"></div>\n  <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.ts\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>","/src/main.ts":"import { createApp } from \"vue\";\nimport App from \"./App.vue\";\ncreateApp(App).mount(\"#example1\");","/src/App.vue":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { ref, useTemplateRef } from 'vue';\nimport { HotTable } from '@handsontable/vue3';\nimport { registerAllModules } from 'handsontable/registry';\nimport { HyperFormula } from 'hyperformula';\nimport type { GridSettings } from 'handsontable/settings';\n\nregisterAllModules();\n\nconst SAMPLE_URL = '/docs/scripts/xlsx/employees.xlsx';\n\nconst hotRef = useTemplateRef<InstanceType<typeof HotTable>>('hotRef');\nconst status = ref('');\n\nconst hotData = [\n  ['Ana García', 'Engineering', 'Senior Engineer', 98000, true, '2022-03-14'],\n  ['James Okafor', 'Marketing', 'Marketing Manager', 87500, true, '2021-07-01'],\n  ['Li Wei', 'Engineering', 'Product Manager', 104000, false, '2020-11-23'],\n  ['Priya Nair', 'Sales', 'Account Executive', 76200, true, '2023-01-09'],\n  ['Tom Bakker', 'Support', 'Support Specialist', 58900, true, '2019-05-30'],\n];\n\n// `hotSettings` stays one stable `ref` that nothing changes after an import. A new settings object,\n// or a change to one of its keys, makes the wrapper send `colHeaders` and `columns` to\n// `updateSettings` again, which puts the sample headers and column types over the imported rows.\nconst hotSettings = ref<GridSettings>({\n  data: hotData,\n  colHeaders: ['Name', 'Department', 'Job title', 'Salary ($)', 'Active', 'Hire date'],\n  columns: [\n    { type: 'text' },\n    { type: 'dropdown', source: ['Engineering', 'Marketing', 'Sales', 'Support'] },\n    { type: 'text' },\n    { type: 'numeric', numericFormat: { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD', minimumFractionDigits: 2 } },\n    { type: 'checkbox' },\n    { type: 'date', dateFormat: { year: 'numeric', month: '2-digit', day: '2-digit' } },\n  ],\n  rowHeaders: true,\n  formulas: { engine: HyperFormula },\n  comments: true,\n  mergeCells: true,\n  hiddenColumns: true,\n  customBorders: true,\n  height: 'auto',\n  autoWrapRow: true,\n  autoWrapCol: true,\n  importFile: true,\n  licenseKey: 'non-commercial-and-evaluation',\n});\n\nasync function importWorkbook(blob: Blob, name: string): Promise<void> {\n  const importPlugin = hotRef.value?.hotInstance?.getPlugin('importFile');\n\n  if (!importPlugin) {\n    status.value = 'The grid is not ready.';\n\n    return;\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const result = await importPlugin.importFromBlob('xlsx', blob, {\n      colHeaders: 'firstRow',\n      importStyles: true,\n    });\n\n    status.value = `Imported ${name}`;\n    console.log('Dropped features:', result.dropped);\n  } catch (error) {\n    // A refused file (an .xls, a password-protected or damaged workbook) rejects with a message\n    // that says what to do; the grid keeps its data.\n    status.value = (error as Error).message;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function loadSample(): Promise<void> {\n  const response = await fetch(SAMPLE_URL);\n\n  await importWorkbook(await response.blob(), 'employees.xlsx');\n}\n\nasync function importFile(event: Event): Promise<void> {\n  const input = event.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const file = input.files?.[0];\n\n  if (file) {\n    await importWorkbook(file, file.name);\n  }\n\n  // Cleared either way, so picking the same file again fires `change` again.\n  input.value = '';\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div id=\"example1\">\n    <div class=\"example-controls-container\">\n      <div class=\"controls\">\n        <button @click=\"loadSample\">Load sample</button>\n        <label for=\"import-file\">Import XLSX</label>\n        <input type=\"file\" id=\"import-file\" accept=\".xlsx\" @change=\"importFile\">\n        <output role=\"status\">{{ status }}</output>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <HotTable ref=\"hotRef\" :settings=\"hotSettings\" />\n  </div>\n</template>"},"docsPath":"guides/accessories-and-menus/import-from-excel/vue/example1.vue","breadcrumb":["Accessories And Menus","Import from Excel"],"guide":"guides/accessories-and-menus/import-from-excel/import-from-excel.md","guideTitle":"Import from Excel","exampleId":"example1","exampleTitle":"Standard example","docPermalink":"/import-from-excel","lang":"Vue 3"}
